  "language": "en",
  "text": "Mid-course test, track one. OK. Today I want you to tell the class about your family at home. Marius, do you have a brother or sister? Yes, I have a brother. He's 14 and he loves football and basketball, and he goes to the gym on Saturday mornings with our father. They both love exercise, but I don't. I like to play computer games. Yes, we know you do. What about you, Clara? I have a big sister and a little brother. My sister Katja likes school. She does her homework after school and then she reads books about science. She wants to study science at university. My brother is five years old and watches TV every evening after school. Sofia, do you have a brother? No, I have one sister Rosa. She's 23 and lives in Mexico with my grandparents. She's at university in Mexico City. Rosa wants to be a doctor and work in a hospital. She goes online and chats to my mother every evening, but she's very busy so they don't chat for a long time. And Jason, what about your family? My parents live in Beijing in China. My father is a chef and he works in a restaurant in the city centre. My mother is a school teacher. They are both very busy, but my mother texts me every day. Do you have any brothers or sisters, Jason? No, I don't.",
